: \"RANKL combined with miR-143 mimics\", \"endpoint\": \"osteoclast formation / positive level of osteoclasts\"} Sign is an inferred normal molecular role; genetic perturbation is not equivalent to pharmacological inhibition. Uncertainties: The quote says 'TARCP staining' rather than a standardized assay name; it was retained as written. | miR-143 molecular form and the exact species context are not explicitly stated in the abstract, though the cell line is mouse-derived and the paper concerns mouse macrophage RAW264.7 cells.", legacy_experiment_id: "", legacy_source_records: ""};
