retained in data/staging/full_integration_v1. Not expert reviewed. {\"directness\": \"unknown\", \"intervention\": \"Bmi1 deficiency; Chk2 knockout\", \"endpoint\": \"osteoclastic bone resorption\"} Sign is an inferred normal molecular role; genetic perturbation is not equivalent to pharmacological inhibition. Uncertainties: The abstract reports osteoclastic bone resorption and marker changes in the same passage; TRAP and RANKL/OPG are treated as readouts rather than direct mechanistic targets.", legacy_experiment_id: "", legacy_source_records: ""};
