\", \"intervention\": \"Mkrn1 overexpression using a retrovirus or silencing using small interfering RNA (siRNA) in bone marrow-derived macrophages (BMMs)\", \"endpoint\": \"osteoclast differentiation\"} Sign is an inferred normal molecular role; genetic perturbation is not equivalent to pharmacological inhibition. Uncertainties: The passage combines overexpression and siRNA experiments; the causal details for each direction are summarized together. | The exact molecular form of MKRN1 is inferred from gene tagging and phosphorylation context, but the text does not explicitly distinguish gene versus protein for every mention.", legacy_experiment_id: "", legacy_source_records: ""};
