egration_v2. Not expert reviewed. {\"directness\": \"unknown\", \"intervention\": \"small interfering RNA-mediated knockdown of Ctdnep1\", \"endpoint\": \"osteoclast differentiation / TRAP-positive multinucleated osteoclasts and marker gene expression\"} Sign is an inferred normal molecular role; genetic perturbation is not equivalent to pharmacological inhibition. Uncertainties: The text links the observation to RANKL-induced RAW264.7 cells, but the species is not explicitly stated in the supplied passage. | Ctdnep1 is treated as a gene-level perturbation target here; the text also refers to the phosphatase protein, so molecular form is not fully disambiguated. | The title states negative regulation, but the extracted claim is limited to the observed knockdown effect and does not assert direct mechanism.", legacy_experiment_id: "", legacy_source_records: ""};
