\": \"deletion of Tlr4\", \"endpoint\": \"osteoclast formation\"} Sign is an inferred normal molecular role; genetic perturbation is not equivalent to pharmacological inhibition. Uncertainties: The text links Tlr4 deletion to both reduced osteoclast formation and reduced expression of NFATc1, CTSK, and TRAP, but does not establish direct regulation versus indirect downstream effects.", legacy_experiment_id: "", legacy_source_records: ""};
